Implement __init__.py re-exports and __all__ package-level dead code

- Parse `__all__ = [...]` into Export symbols linked (ReExport) to their
  definitions; exports are seeded as public-API reachability roots, so
  declared-public names are never classified as bloat.
- Treat `__init__.py` as a package root entrypoint; its top-level imports
  are re-exports that flow reachability to submodule definitions.
- Only __init__.py gets the module->import reachability edge; ordinary
  modules still flag unused imports (preserves unused-import detection).
- Exports are skipped in bloat classification (structural/public).
- Core analysis seeds reachability from exports as public API roots.
- 4 package integration tests: re-export reachability, __all__ protects
  public members, export->definition linking, package-level dead code.
- New example fixture examples/python-pkg.
